\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Evaluation overview. (a) Construction: a LUMIERE glioblastoma case becomes items through automated segmentation, fact extraction from the images, masks and records, stratified sampling of one follow-up, and item assembly; the keys have four origins (AIA sequence, LIL and DSCR segmentation, PJRF outcome, TCM rule). (b) The item instantiates a five-phase same-patient chain; the image-dependent phases (AIA, LIL, DSCR) carry the keys tested here and AIA is the positive control. (c) Each image-dependent phase is run under three controlled input conditions, the patient's own image, text only, and a donor-image swap, giving an accuracy benefit, a response-sensitivity baseline, and a donor-tracking measure; these feed the statistical tests and the image-dependence-versus-response-sensitivity verdict. A reference model is a positive control alongside the four open-weight models.}}{3}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{3}{Evaluation overview. (a) Construction: a LUMIERE glioblastoma case becomes items through automated segmentation, fact extraction from the images, masks and records, stratified sampling of one follow-up, and item assembly; the keys have four origins (AIA sequence, LIL and DSCR segmentation, PJRF outcome, TCM rule). (b) The item instantiates a five-phase same-patient chain; the image-dependent phases (AIA, LIL, DSCR) carry the keys tested here and AIA is the positive control. (c) Each image-dependent phase is run under three controlled input conditions, the patient's own image, text only, and a donor-image swap, giving an accuracy benefit, a response-sensitivity baseline, and a donor-tracking measure; these feed the statistical tests and the image-dependence-versus-response-sensitivity verdict. A reference model is a positive control alongside the four open-weight models}{figure.caption.1}{}}
